# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the studio image's build context
# (infra/studio-cloudbuild.yaml). Presence of this file means .gitignore is NOT
# consulted -- list every heavy/irrelevant path explicitly.
#
# READ THAT SECOND SENTENCE AS A SECURITY PROPERTY, NOT A CONVENIENCE NOTE (ADR-0544).
# apps/studio/Dockerfile is `COPY . .`, so whatever survives this filter is baked into
# a published image, unread. Because .gitignore is bypassed here, a path being
# gitignored buys NOTHING -- every credential-shaped path must be repeated below or it
# ships. This file, not a .dockerignore, is the control: there is no .dockerignore and
# none is wanted, because the documented build path is `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# The exposure this guards is the BY-HAND build (the runbook in studio-cloudbuild.yaml's
# header), which uploads a working tree as it actually is. The CI path
# (.github/workflows/deploy-studio.yml) checks out clean, so only committed files exist
# there and this filter has nothing private to catch.

# -- Credential + private runtime material: the reason this file is security-relevant --
# Mirrors .gitignore's "Env / secrets" block line for line. .env.example tells you to
# copy it to .env and paste an API key in, and .gitignore then makes that feel safe.
# It is only safe here because of the next three lines. Keep the two lists in step.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# App-owned runtime state holding member identities (ADR-0043/0044). Gitignored, never
# committed, and must not be baked into a published image either.
apps/studio/data/users.json
apps/studio/data/attestations.json

# -- Heavy / irrelevant --
.git
.gitmodules
legacy/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.claude/
apps/studio/dist/
apps/studio/.studio.log
apps/studio/.studio.pid
apps/studio/test-results/
apps/studio/playwright-report/
infra/functions/
infra/.terraform/
